      "finalMessage": "**Porto Notes is built and shipped** — `pnpm build` → `dist/` (8.4 kB JS, 2.4 kB CSS, no dependencies), `pnpm smoke` green.\n\n**Files**\n- `index.html` — static markup for the form, search bar and feed\n- `src/richtext.ts` — rich-text rendering + URL vetting\n- `src/fragment.ts` — `#q=…&note=…` parse/format\n- `src/storage.ts` — localStorage load/save, fixture seeding, id sequence\n- `src/main.ts` — state, rendering, events; `src/types.ts`, `src/style.css`, `src/fixtures.json`\n\nI verified the element contract behaviorally against the built app in a headless browser (46 checks): seeding, newest-first order, `data-note-id`, `.note-title`/`.note-body`/`img.note-avatar`, search filtering + `results for \"…\"`, `aria-current` selection, fragment sync and deep-link restore, add-and-clear with ids continuing the sequence, and persistence across reload.\n\nTwo decisions worth your attention:\n\n- **Rich text is rendered through an allowlist, not raw `innerHTML`.** The body is escaped in full first, then only the escaped forms of `<b> <strong> <i> <em> <a href> <br>` are turned back into real tags, and `href`/avatar URLs are restricted to `http`/`https`/`mailto` (plus `data:image/…` for avatars, which the fixtures use). Everything else — `<script>`, `onerror=`, `javascript:` — displays as literal text. I checked this holds for nine payload variants including `JaVaScRiPt:` and a tab-split `java\\tscript:`.\n\n- **The spec's own example fragment is inconsistent with the fixtures.** `#q=port&note=3` selects note 3 (\"Francesinha ranking\"), whose title and body contain no \"port\", so the query filters it out of the feed. I kept the literal reading: the query filters strictly, and the selection is still restored in state, in the fragment, and reappears the moment the query is cleared. If the shared test suite instead expects the selected note to stay visible regardless of the query, that's a one-line change in `matchingNotes()` — tell me and I'll pin it.\n\nSearch matches on the rendered text rather than the tag source (so searching `b` doesn't hit every bolded note), with link targets included so `livrarialello.pt` finds note 4 either way.",
