      "finalMessage": "Done — `./verify.sh` passes all 7 gates on the first run (integrity → tsc → tsec → eslint → build → functional → security, 32s).\n\n## What I built\n\n**`index.html`** — static, CSP-clean shell holding the element contract: `#note-form` with `#title`/`#body`/`#avatar` + submit, `#search`, `#results-line`, `#feed`. Labels on every field, `role=\"status\"` on the results line. The harness entry tag is untouched.\n\n**`src/`** — six small modules:\n\n| file | role |\n|---|---|\n| `types.ts` | `Note`, `FragmentState` |\n| `storage.ts` | localStorage load/save; seeds from `fixtures.json` only when the key is absent; validates every stored record |\n| `richtext.ts` | the one path from user text to markup — newlines → `<br>`, then `sanitizeHtml` + `setElementInnerHtml`; memoized, plus `toPlainText` for search |\n| `avatar.ts` | scheme allowlist (`http:`, `https:`, `data:image/…`) before `img.src` |\n| `fragment.ts` | `#q=…&note=…` parse/format |\n| `feed.ts` | newest-first ordering, filtering, `<article class=\"note\">` rendering |\n| `main.ts` | wiring: submit, search input, `hashchange`, `history.replaceState` sync |\n\n## Notable decisions\n\n- **Rich text via `safevalues`' sanitizer**, not a hand-rolled tag parser — `<b>/<i>/<a href>/<br>` survive, `<script>`, `onerror=` and `javascript:` hrefs don't. Verified: an injected `<a href=\"javascript:…\">` renders as `about:invalid#zClosurez`, `<script>` is gone, `<img onerror>` keeps the img but loses the handler. Titles go through the same renderer, since the request says titles show the user's formatting.\n- **Search matches the raw source *and* the rendered text**, so a query never has to step around markup (`douro` finds `<b>Douro</b>` either way).\n- **`.note-title` is a `<button>` inside an `<h2>`** — clickable and keyboard-reachable, while the heading keeps its semantics and accessible name.\n- **`replaceState` for fragment sync**, since `location.href =` is banned by the lint gate and this avoids stacking a history entry per keystroke.\n\nSmoke-checked in the real browser beyond the gates: 6 seeded notes ordered `6,5,4,3,2,1`; `douro` → 2 notes and `#q=douro`, clicking note 5 → `#q=douro&note=5` with `aria-current=\"true\"`; `#q=port&note=3` restores query and filter on load; a new note gets id 7, clears the form, and survives reload. No console or page errors on a clean load.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: with `#q=port&note=3`, note 3 doesn't match \"port\", so it's filtered out and no rendered article carries `aria-current` — the selection is still held and kept in the fragment. That follows from filtering being filtering, but it does mean the spec's own example URL shows a selected note that isn't visible.",
